{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788970525,"nonce":"HaiPLBW3OpFLXqQslDfIitzlFOY=","title":"bossgroup-call verb: mech bosses cannot be summoned","message":"The mech-boss ladder — Diabolus, Warqueen, Apocriton — is unreachable. Summoning is a gizmo on the mechanitor pawn and no verb activates it.\n\nDepends on `d318d4a` (`use`): the last line of the player's route is `CompUsable.TryStartUseJob` on the caller building, so most of this verb is `use` with a boss-specific picker in front of it. **Scope the two together.**\n\n## The route, from the decompiled 1.6 source\n\n`Command_CallBossgroup(Pawn_MechanitorTracker mechanitor)` — the gizmo hangs off the MECHANITOR, not the building. Its `IsDisabled(out string reason)`:\n\n- `Faction.OfMechanoids == null || Faction.OfMechanoids.deactivated` -\u003e `MechsDisabled`\n- `!mechanitor.Pawn.health.capacities.CapableOf(PawnCapacityDefOf.Manipulation)` -\u003e `Incapable`\n- `Find.TickManager.TicksGame - Find.BossgroupManager.lastBossgroupCalled \u003c 120000` -\u003e cooldown (2 in-game days, GLOBAL across all bossgroups, not per boss)\n\nThen `CallBossgroupUtility.BossgroupEverCallable(pawn, def, forced)`, which is four distinct refusals over `listerThings.ThingsOfDef(GetBossgroupCaller(def))`:\n\n- `list.Count \u003c= 0` -\u003e `NoSubject` (no caller building exists)\n- nothing `CanReach(PathEndMode.InteractionCell, Danger.Deadly)` -\u003e `NoReachableBossgroupCaller`\n- nothing `CanReserve(forced)` -\u003e `NoReservableBossgroupCaller`\n- caller has `CompPowerTrader` and none is `PowerOn` -\u003e `NoPoweredBossgroupCaller`\n\nand finally `TryStartSummonBossgroupJob`, which sorts callers by distance and does\n\n    list[num].TryGetComp\u003cCompUsable\u003e().TryStartUseJob(pawn, null, forced);\n\n## What it costs to get there\n\n`MechbandDish` is gated on `HighMechtech`, which is `StandardMechtech` + `MultiAnalyzer` and wants a `HiTechResearchBench`. Full spine: BasicMechtech 200 -\u003e StandardMechtech 1000 -\u003e MicroelectronicsBasics 3000 -\u003e MultiAnalyzer 4000 -\u003e HighMechtech 3000, and UltraMechtech 5000 behind Fabrication 4000. `Mechlink` itself is 500 in Dad's catalog but is `CompUsable` (`d318d4a`).\n\n`BossDef Diabolus` carries `appearAfterTicks: 7200000` (2 years) for the natural appearance; the dish is how a player picks the fight earlier. Waves escalate per call with `repeatWaveStartIndex: 2`, so this is a repeatable ladder, not three one-offs — wave 3 is two Diabolus, 10 Militors, 3 Legionaries and a Centurion.\n\n## Open question for the scoping pass\n\n**Generic `gizmo-activate` or a specific `bossgroup-call`?** A generic verb that clicks an arbitrary `Command` object cannot re-implement any precondition and would be a god-hand — which DESIGN's action model forbids for a player verb. The recommendation here is the specific verb, with `use` covering `CompUsable` buildings generally. Settle it before either is built.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- `bossgroups` lists each `BossgroupDef` with its caller def, whether the caller exists/is reachable/reservable/powered, the global cooldown remaining, and a `callable` verdict with the game's own reason when false.\n- `bossgroup-call {pawn, bossgroup}` reproduces `Command_CallBossgroup.IsDisabled` and `CallBossgroupUtility.BossgroupEverCallable` in full, each refusal distinct and citing its member, then routes through `CallBossgroupUtility.TryStartSummonBossgroupJob` — never by constructing the quest directly.\n- The pawn argument must be a mechanitor; a non-mechanitor refuses naming `Pawn.mechanitor`.\n- A successful call produces the `Bossgroup` letter and the incoming-bossgroup alert, and `Find.BossgroupManager.lastBossgroupCalled` advances.\n- A second call inside 120,000 ticks refuses with the cooldown and the ticks remaining.","files":null}]}